<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="proof-band">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Where the line is</div>
    <h2>It never gives advice about an animal</h2>
    <p>A receptionist can take a booking, capture a breed and repeat your posted policy. It cannot tell someone whether a limp is serious, whether a lump needs looking at, or whether their dog is safe to board — and it doesn't try. Anything that sounds like an animal in trouble goes to a human immediately, with your emergency instructions and nothing else attached.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No medical opinions, ever</strong>
        <span>Symptoms, injuries, reactions and "should I be worried" go straight to you or to your posted emergency instructions. It never assesses an animal.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No blind quotes</strong>
        <span>It captures breed, size, coat and condition and explains what moves the price. The number is yours, given once you've seen the animal.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Your policies, word for word</strong>
        <span>Vaccination requirements, temperament rules, cancellation and late-pickup policy — repeated exactly as you've published them, never improvised.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Holiday surge, same coverage</strong>
        <span>It doesn't get overwhelmed when the whole town calls about Christmas boarding in the same week. The fortieth caller gets the same answer as the first.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

